===== CAPTION TEXT =====
A: Figure 30: The three eigenmodes that carry the largest shares of each sixteen-cell prediction’s χ2 (columns, by rank), for GENIE CV, GENIE + MEC, NuWro and MINERvA Tune v1 (rows), from the reported comparison on Ctotal + Cresp + Vg relative to f . The bars are each mode’s unit loadings on R00–R15, signed so that the largest loading is positive. Each panel gives the mode’s share of the χ2 , its relative σ and the prediction’s distance along it, the projection over σ. The residual is (f − g)/f , so a positive distance means that the data lie above the prediction along the mode as signed. GiBUU, compared on 8 cells, has no modes here.
B: FIG. 5. Categorical breakdown of systematic uncertainties on the double-differential cross section measurement in slices of p|| (top) and pT (bottom). Flux is the dominant uncertainty in the majority of phase space, with muon reconstruction the other comparable uncertainty in some areas.
